# Shell scripts and systemd units must always have LF line endings, regardless
# of a contributor's global core.autocrlf setting — a CRLF shebang line breaks
# a script outright on Linux ("bad interpreter: No such file or directory"),
# and deployment/install.sh + deployment/systemd/apex.service (RM-AIM-P3
# DEP-301) are Linux-only artifacts that could otherwise be silently corrupted
# by a checkout on Windows.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
